                <pb facs="0381" n="375" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg375"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic">June 21,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that this Government is opposed to raising the revenue above 5
                    per cent effective, but directs Mr. Rockhill to refrain from opposing
                    proposition of eventual discussion if it will aid in bringing negotiations to a
                    close.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
